{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgfwKSwV7a8Fdpbpo3ET4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fit gives Dq = 1750 cm⁻¹, B = 618 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 2490 cm⁻¹. I got Dq and B from the three spin-allowed bands and C from the spin-forbidden band.\n\n**Dq from the first band.** The lowest spin-allowed band is ⁴A₂g → ⁴T₂g, and its energy is Δ = 10Dq. So 10Dq = 17 500 cm⁻¹ and Dq = 1750 cm⁻¹.\n\n**B from the other two bands.** The two ⁴T₁g levels, ⁴T₁g(F) and ⁴T₁g(P), satisfy ν₂ + ν₃ = 15B + 3Δ.\n- 23 860 + 37 910 = 61 770 cm⁻¹, and 3Δ = 52 500 cm⁻¹.\n- This gives 15B = 9270 cm⁻¹, so B = 618 cm⁻¹.\n- Check: ν₃ − ν₂ should equal √(225B² + Δ² − 18BΔ). With B = 618 this is about 14 054 cm⁻¹, against 14 050 cm⁻¹ observed.\n\n**C from the sharp band.** The lowest spin-forbidden transition is ⁴A₂g → ²Eg. I took the weak sharp band at 12 090 cm⁻¹ to be this one. The sharp band is C-dependent, so I diagonalised the full d³ matrix at Dq = 1750 cm⁻¹ and B = 618 cm⁻¹.\n- A quick estimate, E(²Eg) ≈ 9B + 3C − 90B²/Δ, suggested C ≈ 2830 cm⁻¹. The full calculation put ²Eg at 13 116 cm⁻¹ for C = 2831 cm⁻¹, which is too high, so I discarded that estimate.\n- Lowering C to 2490 cm⁻¹ puts ²Eg at 12 077 cm⁻¹, which matches the observed 12 090 cm⁻¹.\n- The same calculation reproduces the spin-allowed bands at 17 500, 23 858 and 37 912 cm⁻¹. The ²T₁g level lies slightly higher, at 12 621 cm⁻¹.\n\nThe resulting C/B is about 4.0.\n\n{\"Dq\": 1750, \"B\": 618, \"C\": 2490, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Dq from ν1, B from ν2+ν3 relation, C from full d3 matrix fit of the 2Eg level to 12090 cm-1.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2221,"cache_read_input_tokens":10847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2221,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":887,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","spe